        "original_id": "2202c36d-185e-5212-b01d-efa48d41bba4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fetteresso Castle, Cowie Castle, Catterline, Cowie Water, Aberdeenshire, Scotland\n- Topics: architecture, historic features, prehistoric use\n\nFacts:\n- Fetteresso Castle is a 14th-century towerhouse that was rebuilt in 1761 as a Scottish Gothic-style Palladian manor.\n- Fetteresso Castle shows clear evidence of prehistoric use of its site.\n- Cowie Castle is a ruined fortress in Aberdeenshire, Scotland.\n- In the general area of Catterline, noted architectural or historic features include Fetteresso Castle, Fiddes Castle, the Chapel of St. Mary and St. Nathalan, and Muchalls Castle.\n- Cowie Water is south of the ruined Cowie Castle.",
